class Solution {

    // Recursive function that returns the carry (0 or 1)
    static int helper(Node temp) {

        // Base case:
        // If we've moved past the last node,
        // return 1 because we need to add one to the number.
        if (temp == null)
            return 1;

        // Go to the next node first.
        // This makes recursion reach the last digit.
        int carry = helper(temp.next);

        // Add the carry returned from the next node.
        temp.data = temp.data + carry;

        // If the digit is less than 10,
        // there is no carry.
        if (temp.data < 10)
            return 0;

        // If the digit becomes 10,
        // store 0 in the current node.
        temp.data = 0;

        // Return carry = 1 to the previous node.
        return 1;
    }

    public static Node addOne(Node head) {

        // Call helper() on the entire linked list.
        // It updates all node values and returns
        // the final carry.
        int carry = helper(head);

        // If carry is still 1,
        // create a new node at the beginning.
        if (carry == 1) {

            Node newNode = new Node(1);

            // Connect the new node to the old head.
            newNode.next = head;

            // New node becomes the new head.
            return newNode;
        }

        // If carry is 0,
        // simply return the updated list.
        return head;
    }
}
| Complexity           | Value    | Reason                                                  |
| -------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Time Complexity  | O(n) | Every node is visited exactly once.                     |
| Space Complexity | O(n) | Recursive call stack stores one function call per node. |
